## OPERATING RULES FOR THE AGENT

- Never guess API behavior for Spring Boot 4.1 / Spring 7 / JDK 21 — verify against official
  Spring and OpenJDK release notes/migration guides before applying a change; if uncertain,
  flag the file as "needs human review" rather than making an unverified change.
- Never mark a file "Migrated - Verified" without: (a) compiling, (b) passing tests,
  (c) passing SonarQube quality gate, (d) passing SAST scan.
- Never suppress a static analysis or security finding without a documented justification
  reviewed by a human; suppression is not a substitute for fixing the root cause.
- Prefer minimal, reviewable diffs over speculative refactors.
- Escalate (stop and ask) whenever a change would alter externally observable API contracts,
  security posture, or persisted data formats.
- Keep an audit trail: every file's status must be traceable back to the specific migration
  driver (JDK21 / Boot4.1 / Spring7 / transitive dependency) that required the change.

